[[12,1,0,"<h2>STRUCTURE</h2><p>The engine is connected at the top to the bodyshell by means of a reaction rod in order to contain jolting.</p><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/33852.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><ul class=\"legend\"><li>1. Power unit rigid rear support.</li><li>2. Power unit rigid rear support flexible mounting.</li><li>3. Power unit reaction rod.</li><li>4. Power unit rigid front support flexible mounting.</li><li>5. Rigid engine support, timing side.</li><li>6. Power unit rigid rear support, gearbox side.</li></ul></figure>"]]